e: notable situations\n- **Cheeky Nando's (aCaps)** carries two banged-up starters: Mike Evans (hip, \"will have to be managed\" per his coach, expected to play but monitor practice reps, NBC Sports Sept 21) and Malik Nabers (shoulder popped out and back in vs. the Rams, said he's \"OK\" pending X-rays, Yahoo Sports Sept 21-22). Not a trade target this week given the uncertainty.\n- **Saquon Barkley (Eazy E Squad)** is dealing with a stinger, not a structural injury; reports suggest he has a real chance to play Week 3 (multiple outlets, Sept 22-23).\n- **J.K. Dobbins (City of Champyinz)** has a hamstring issue but was called \"good\" to go by Tom Pelissero for this week (Sept 22).\n- Three rivals (Amateur Hour/Rome Odunze, Baker's Dozen/Tee Higgins, Be Safe Get Jaxcinated/Chris Olave) are shown starting a WR at a projected 0.0 \u2014 worth a look as bye-week or return-package trade fits ahead of the Week 12 deadline, but no urgency yet.\n\n## Bottom line (3 bullets max)\n- Watch Dowdle's Friday practice report; if he's out, plug in Woody Marks, not George Holani.\n- Put your FAAB weight behind Travis Kelce at $22; the other TEs are all just quarter-value depth, don't overspend on a second one.\n- No trades to make this week; keep an eye on the three 0.0-projected rival WRs as future trade bait.\n",
